{"ts":"2026-09-10T21:51:51.608Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"6a8f89476c713afa8ad564ae","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-10T21:51:51.608Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-09-10T21:51:51.608Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Design: Added content-defined chunking (CDC) using a Gear rolling hash with a deterministic 256-entry table. CDC picks boundaries from the hash, so inserting bytes near the front perturbs only the fragments around the edit. Both modes coexist: fixed-size for computable range reads, CDC for reuse under edit. The mode is recorded in the manifest (mode cdc line, backward-compatible with existing fixed manifests). \n\nCDC parameters (justified by npm run benchmark:cdc on a 256 KiB corpus with 64-byte edits):\n- minChunkSize=512, maxChunkSize=65536, mask=0x1fff (13-bit, ~8 KiB avg)\n- Front insertion reuse: CDC 95% vs fixed-size 0% (all fragments shift)\n- Middle: CDC 95%, End: CDC 95%\n- Memory bounded by maxChunkSize (verified by streaming memory test)\n- Determinism verified in-process and across processes\n\nThe benchmark script (scripts/cdc-benchmark.ts) is excluded from the coverage gate as a reproducibility tool, not production code."}]}],"before_hash":"9bfe5f17f66ebcafca6a83b191cdfdab19ef3d91640246b37ebefb5ed97a4d18","after_hash":"61b09ea727c8bd2f011d59c148d3756e1a319fc7eaac489bec4067e8fb0f6c60","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"5bb2028698db008dc5c34c9c962c4d1832fcc22f839c4e319b29f3874d6c2073"}
